{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246140",
      "title": "Understanding React Server Components",
      "sourceHash": "03259a17e295bc1f7d16b2ec9e74b6739aac472b4b290403899d71a3adbdbb52",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "So React has some features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 10.11,
          "en": "that are part of React and that are marked as stable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.11,
          "end": 14.1,
          "en": "that can't be used in every React project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.1,
          "end": 16.86,
          "en": "and therefore you need special project setups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 19.11,
          "en": "like the one you get from Next.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.11,
          "end": 22.11,
          "en": "which does support running some code on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.11,
          "end": 25.17,
          "en": "and running some code on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.17,
          "end": 29.04,
          "en": "And, therefore, let's start by taking a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.04,
          "end": 32.79,
          "en": "at this React Server Components feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 34.41,
          "en": "because that's a big one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.41,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "That's an important React feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 41.19,
          "en": "even though you might not be able to use it in all projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.19,
          "end": 45.6,
          "en": "But understanding React Server Components is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.6,
          "end": 46.86,
          "en": "And it's also important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.86,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "to understand the difference compared to Client Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 53.49,
          "en": "which is kind of the opposite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.49,
          "end": 55.413,
          "en": "kind of components you can build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 60.51,
          "en": "And React Server Components, as the name kind of implies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.51,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "are components that are never executed on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "So those component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 69.48,
          "en": "never execute on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.48,
          "end": 71.58,
          "en": "Indeed, the code of these components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.58,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "never makes it to the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 79.34,
          "en": "Instead, these component functions are executed on a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.83,
          "end": 82.41,
          "en": "or actually during the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.41,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "if they are pre-rendered, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 88.08,
          "en": "but they're never executed on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.08,
          "end": 91.14,
          "en": "Now, client components on the other hand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.14,
          "end": 96.14,
          "en": "are rendered on the client side, but not just there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.3,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "They are instead also rendered on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 101.72999999999999,
          "en": "They are pre-rendered there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.72999999999999,
          "end": 104.91,
          "en": "when a request hits the server, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.91,
          "end": 108.12,
          "en": "so that the finished HTML page is sent back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.12,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "as part of the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "but then thereafter they run again on the client side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 117.42,
          "en": "and you get a single page application thereafter, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.42,
          "end": 121.53,
          "en": "where users can then interact with a client side React app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 124.98,
          "en": "and where you can therefore use client side features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.98,
          "end": 128.79,
          "en": "like the useState hook or something like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.79,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "which would not be possible in server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "But let's simply take a look at that in practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 139.863,
          "en": "in this demo project, which I shared in the last lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.88,
          "end": 142.68,
          "en": "Here in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.68,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "I have a very simple Next.js application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.74,
          "end": 148.23,
          "en": "which doesn't contain any components yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 151.666,
          "en": "Basically, it just has this page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.666,
          "end": 155.67000000000002,
          "en": "which is pretty empty, but now we'll add some components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.67000000000002,
          "end": 158.04,
          "en": "And, therefore, I'll add a components folder here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.04,
          "end": 160.41,
          "en": "to the main project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.41,
          "end": 164.7,
          "en": "and attached you then find two component files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.7,
          "end": 169.41,
          "en": "You find an RSCDemo.js file attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.41,
          "end": 172.47,
          "en": "which you should store in your components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.47,
          "end": 176.4,
          "en": "And you find a ClientDemo.js file attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.4,
          "end": 179.883,
          "en": "which you should also store in your components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.72,
          "end": 185.43,
          "en": "Now, both component files contain regular React components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.43,
          "end": 188.043,
          "en": "There's nothing special about them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.09,
          "end": 192.21,
          "en": "And if you now go to this page.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.21,
          "end": 196.59,
          "en": "which in the Next.js application in this app folder here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.59,
          "end": 199.65,
          "en": "is responsible for rendering a page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.65,
          "end": 202.77,
          "en": "If you go there, you can use these components in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.77,
          "end": 205.59,
          "en": "because the page.js file also includes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.59,
          "end": 208.07999999999998,
          "en": "just a regular component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.07999999999998,
          "end": 212.621,
          "en": "just a component, which due to this special reserved file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.621,
          "end": 214.44,
          "en": "name will be picked up by Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.44,
          "end": 216.903,
          "en": "and will be rendered to the page automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.25,
          "end": 222.48,
          "en": "So in here we could now output the RSCDemo component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.48,
          "end": 225.72,
          "en": "which is imported from that components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.72,
          "end": 229.77,
          "en": "And this @ symbol here is a special import alias,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.77,
          "end": 232.8,
          "en": "which is supported in Next.js projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.8,
          "end": 235.86,
          "en": "which simply refers to the root project folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.86,
          "end": 239.04,
          "en": "so that we import this from the RSCDemo file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.04,
          "end": 240.74,
          "en": "which is in the components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.589,
          "end": 243.72,
          "en": "which is in the root project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.72,
          "end": 247.29,
          "en": "And then I output this RSCDemo component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.29,
          "end": 250.98,
          "en": "And if you do that and you reload the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.98,
          "end": 255.57,
          "en": "that's served by that development server on localhost:3000,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.57,
          "end": 258.363,
          "en": "you should see this component on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.89,
          "end": 262.38,
          "en": "And what's interesting now is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.38,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "that if you open the developer tools here in your browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.26,
          "en": "and you reload maybe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 268.26,
          "end": 273.183,
          "en": "you never see this log message there in the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.29,
          "end": 277.29,
          "en": "so that's not logged in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.29,
          "end": 279.36,
          "en": "Instead, you can see it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 279.36,
          "end": 282.09000000000003,
          "en": "if you open the terminal or command prompt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 282.09000000000003,
          "end": 285.09000000000003,
          "en": "which you used to start that development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.09000000000003,
          "end": 288.33299999999997,
          "en": "because there it's being logged.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 292.32,
          "en": "So this log message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 292.32,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "is showing up in this terminal here in this log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 301.23,
          "en": "And messages that show up here are printed by the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 301.23,
          "end": 305.25,
          "en": "So they are output on the server side, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.25,
          "end": 307.23,
          "en": "and that proves that this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 307.23,
          "end": 309.12,
          "en": "is rendered on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 309.12,
          "end": 312.84,
          "en": "Now, you might say there's nothing special",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 312.84,
          "end": 314.01,
          "en": "about this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 314.01,
          "end": 316.29,
          "en": "It looks like any other component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.29,
          "end": 320.07,
          "en": "from one of the many other sections you saw in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.07,
          "end": 321.48,
          "en": "and you would be right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 321.48,
          "end": 324.33,
          "en": "This is a regular React component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.33,
          "end": 327.24,
          "en": "So what turns this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 327.24,
          "end": 330.63,
          "en": "into a React Server Component then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 330.63,
          "end": 333.81,
          "en": "And the answer is, as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 333.81,
          "end": 338.81,
          "en": "the special project setup that is provided by Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 340.38,
          "end": 343.59000000000003,
          "en": "Next.js projects are set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 348.59000000000003,
          "en": "such that all React components by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 348.72,
          "end": 351.15,
          "en": "are treated as server components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 351.15,
          "end": 354.78,
          "en": "which means they are never rendered on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 354.78,
          "end": 357.9,
          "en": "They are always rendered on the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 357.9,
          "end": 359.31,
          "en": "And that's, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 359.31,
          "end": 363.51,
          "en": "not the case when using a Vite-based project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 363.51,
          "end": 366.42,
          "en": "There you get a client-side React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 366.42,
          "end": 368.43,
          "en": "as a default instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 368.43,
          "end": 372.15,
          "en": "So that's why this is a server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 372.15,
          "end": 376.65,
          "en": "And, similarly, if you take a look at this client demo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 376.65,
          "end": 380.4,
          "en": "this also actually at the moment still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 380.4,
          "end": 382.65,
          "en": "is a React Server Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 382.65,
          "end": 386.343,
          "en": "because it's also just a regular React component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 387.39,
          "end": 390.39,
          "en": "So if we output that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 390.39,
          "end": 393.96,
          "en": "maybe below the RSCDemo component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 393.96,
          "end": 397.17,
          "en": "and you reload, you can see that component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 397.17,
          "end": 399.843,
          "en": "but you see no log here in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 401.49,
          "end": 403.29,
          "en": "And instead you see this message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 403.29,
          "end": 405.633,
          "en": "here in the server side log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 407.22,
          "end": 410.85,
          "en": "So this is no client component yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 410.85,
          "end": 412.29,
          "en": "It's a server component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 412.29,
          "end": 415.86,
          "en": "because by default in Next projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 415.86,
          "end": 420.86,
          "en": "and actually in all projects that support server components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 421.17,
          "end": 424.95,
          "en": "components are server components out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 424.95,
          "end": 428.37,
          "en": "And if you wanna change them to client components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 428.37,
          "end": 432.09,
          "en": "you have to tell React and this project setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 432.09,
          "end": 434.253,
          "en": "And that's what we'll do next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}